## VERDICT
## **ACCEPT** 7.1 walker memory/perf honesty
SPRINT **7.1** (`c_guard_scan_idents` — no per-char OoStr concat / “stack
buffer”) is **true on source and on the live product host**:

1. **Source walker** (`ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret_guard.oo` `c_guard_scan_idents`):
   **zero** `name = name + c` / `out = out +` / `ident = ident +`. Ident
   span is **one** `str_slice(args, start, i)` then refuse.
2. **Host is not stale for the 7.1 body.** Product `ooda/oodac/oodac`
   (962960 B, md5 `a44ee35e…`, mtime 2026-08-12 07:49:59 -0700) **defines**
   `c_guard_scan_idents` and calls **`oo_str_slice` once, `oo_str_concat`
   zero times** in that function (objdump). Host mtime is **after** the
   slice land (source HEAD already sliced; WT extras are `__sec_sink__`
   on `c_secret_emit_guard` only).
3. **Long-ident / long-arg product pipeline is not hang-free at 10s.**
   Isolated: hang is **not** this walker. `oodac check` of 200-arg
   `println` is **slower** than `emit-c` — check never calls
   `c_guard_scan_idents`. Long idents pay `try_scan_ident` `id = id + c2`
   (lexer; not 7.1).

**Do not claim:** product emit/check O(n) or ≤10s for N≥200 args or
ident length ≥16k; 7.10 closed; lexer ident scan sliced.

**Do not REJECT 7.1** solely because WT `c_secret_emit_guard` grew
`__sec_sink__` after host build — 7.1 slice body is identical HEAD↔WT↔host.

